  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ARIJ-FAIR4ALL Trade &amp; Value Chains</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project influencing idea focuses on creating a more comprehensive understanding of the impact of Israeli military orders and occupation practices on the economic empowerment and livelihood of Palestinian rural women and explore ways to strengthen their resilience in the West Bank. By raising awareness among affected rural women towards their rights, become more resilient in their lands and to advocate against the settlers attacks and the Occupation practices.  This will be achieved through applying smart ways of researching and documentation based on data collection and witnessed facts on the ground through telling stories, media and social media engagement, community and stakeholders&#x2019; engagement, networking and alliances, public awareness, policy and legal advocacy, etc.  Theimportance of this project is evident given based on the following two facts: 1. Israeli military orders effect, and 2. the settlers&#x2019; violence effect in the West Bank.  Accordingly, the Israeli government&apos;s recent emphasis on intensifying settlement activities inthe West Bank and supporting settlers&apos; attacks on Palestinian lands, water resources, and crops. These actions pose a significant threat to the livelihoods and food security of the Palestinian people, particularly those engaged in women-led agriculture and their families.

RIJ houses a robust Geo-informatics and settlement-monitoring department that monitors and meticulously documents Israelisettlement activities, with a specific focus on agriculture and natural resources. This is achieved through the adapt use of Satellite and aerial photos, employing advanced GIS and RS technology. The department diligently follows issued military orders related toland confiscation, providing comprehensive insights into the evolving landscape.
Additionally, ARIJ is committed to documenting settlers&apos; attacks on Palestinian lands and resources through a combination of field surveys and official news sources. This multi-faceted approach ensures a nuanced understanding of the challenges faced.</narrative>
  </description>
